From 359b51bcd15eef18dfdb45482367ef43ffcf71c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:20:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Restrict read-only diagnostics to local single-player

Several read-only queries disclosed host information to whatever client Lua
runs in the client realm. On a remote server that Lua is server-sent, so a
multiplayer client exposed: Interfaces.Resolve (module and vtable addresses),
Interfaces.FileExists (filesystem probing), Engine.ListConsole and
Engine.GetConVar (any convar value), and Lua.Global/Lua.Hooks against the
menu or server realm.

Outside local single-player (the native IsLocalSinglePlayer decision), these
now refuse:
- Interfaces.Resolve, Interfaces.FileExists, Engine.ListConsole: refused
  outright.
- Engine.GetConVar: only rendering convars, by the short case-insensitive
  allowlist Policy::IsRenderingConVar in render_policy.h (rtx*, r_*, mat_*,
  cl_draw*), tested in render_policy_test.cpp.
- Lua.Global and Lua.Hooks: only the module's own client state; other realms
  need single-player.

The read-only client diagnostics and the rtx.* rendering query/config surface
a multiplayer RTX session uses are unchanged. Single-player is still decided
natively from the engine client.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
